@node Common description
@chapter Description of the liteJSON library
There are two modules to work with: liteJSON and @code{JSONValue}.
liteJSON is a main parser and JSON tree container. @code{JSONValue} is a cover
for JSON tree basic entry.

@menu
* liteJSON module::liteJSON module
* JSONValue module::JSONValue module
* liteJSON API::liteJSON API
@end menu

@node liteJSON module
@section liteJSON module
liteJSON contains @code{JSONLoader} class which is main parser class and JSON
tree container. It allows to load JSON file, check it for JSON standard
consistency and then build a JSON tree. Programmer can walk through the tree by
getting root JSON value and check for it's children.

@node JSONValue module
@section JSONValue module
The @code{JSONValue} is used to hold JSON tree or it's subtrees. JSONValue
can be one of six basic data types: @b{null}, @b{string}, @b{number},
@b{boolean}, @b{array} and @b{object}. All this types has different lexical
look and separated by @code{JSONLoader} class at lexical analysis.

The @code{JSONValue} can be checked for it's type. It is assumed that the user
knows the data field type in advance. So when user try to read value of
@code{JSONValue} object, he or she use one of convert functions to extract
raw value of the JSON node. But there is the protection mechanism. For example
if user is trying to get number from string node, there will an error be
thrown. Always check node type if there is some concern about it's real type.

