@node JSONLoader class
@section JSONLoader class
@deftp {Class} JSONLoader
main JSON parser.
@end deftp

@defmethod JSONLoader JSONLoader ()
  This method constructs the new parser without JSON tree. It is used for
  generate user defined JSON tree to save it to the file.
@end defmethod

@defmethod JSONLoader JSONLoader (const std::string& @code{file_name})
  This method constructs the new parser and load it's content from file named
  @var{file_name}. It is try to parse JSON file and build a JSON tree. If
  parsing was fail, the JSON tree will remains empty. There is a @var{bad} flag
  that indicates of some problems with the parsing. The error will be printed
  to @code{stdout}.
@end defmethod

@deftypemethod JSONLoader bool is_bad ()
  This method return the value of the @var{bad} flag. Note, that the @var{bad}
  flag set only during parsing process. So if empty JSON tree is generated,
  the @code{is_bad} return @code{false}.
@end deftypemethod

@deftypemethod JSONLoader void clear_tree ()
  This method allows to clear previously created or loaded JSON tree.
@end deftypemethod

@deftypemethod JSONLoader JSONValue* get_root () const
  This method returns root of the JSON tree. It is used to walk through tree,
  search and extract data.
@end deftypemethod

@node JSONValue class
@section JSONValue class
@deftp {Data Type} JSONValueType
  This is the JSON value type enumerator. It defines one of the six JSON
  node types.

  @float table,table:JSONValueType
    @multitable @columnfractions 0.5 0.5
      @headitem Name @tab Description
      @item @code{Invalid} @tab Reserved for errors
      @item @code{Null} @tab Empty entry with keyword @code{null}
      @item @code{Boolean} @tab Boolean value, that can be @code{true} or
            @code{false}
      @item @code{Number} @tab Any numeric value
      @item @code{String} @tab Text value with quoting
      @item @code{Array} @tab Array value in square brackets, where items
            separated by commas
      @item @code{Object} @tab Set of pairs @samp{name:value} in curved braces
            separated by commas
    @end multitable
  @end float
@end deftp

@deftp {Class} JSONValue
JSON tree node abstract class.
@end deftp

